## Engineering process (neyra-dev-kit)

This repo uses the shared Neyra engineering skill stack. Auto-subagents live in `.claude/agents/` (Claude Code delegates by `description` automatically). Full spec + skill↔subagent map: [AGENTS.neyra-devkit.md](AGENTS.neyra-devkit.md).

**Transparency — required in `/loop` and autonomous runs:** each turn, name the skill(s)/subagent(s) you used or assumed and why. Report subagent results faithfully (distinguish what was verified from what is still assumed). Skip a matrix-required check only with an explicit one-line reason in the same turn.

**Post-implementation gate — before declaring a code slice done:** `code-reviewer` (reuse/scope) → matrix add-ons for the touched surface (`localization-checker` for copy, `contract-checker` for endpoints) → `verify-runtime` on the real surface (`{{BUILD_VERIFY_CMD}}`) → `release-readiness` + `regression-scout` for high-risk or cross-layer changes.

## Self-Improvement Rule

When work surfaces a repeatable mistake, a skipped gate, a gate that fired on a stale input, or a corrected assumption, close the loop via `kit-evolution` (`agents/dev-skills/kit-evolution/SKILL.md`): append one line to `agents/neyra-dev-kit/signals.log` in the same turn, then route it to a skill, an enforced check, a knowledge-graph node, or `settings/lessons.md`.

A signal that lives only in the conversation evaporates. Don't wait for a retro.

**Promoted project lessons live in `settings/lessons.md`, never in this block.** Everything between the kit markers is regenerated on every install — a lesson written here is wiped by the next upgrade. `settings/lessons.md` is repo-owned: the installer seeds it once and never touches it again.

Auto-memory is durable knowledge, not scratch: when work changes a fact you've stored, update its memory node **and** re-stamp `last_verified` in the same turn (the `knowledge-graph` freshness contract — `Owner · Last-verified · drift-vs-code`), so `agents/neyra-dev-kit/knowledge/memory_freshness.py` can sweep it for staleness. An unstamped node rots silently.
